tation, and Building Solutions. The E-Infrastructure Solutions segment provides site development services for the blue-chip end users in the e-commerce distribution center, data center, manufacturing, warehousing, and power generation sectors. Its Transportation Solutions segment is involved in the development of infrastructure and rehabilitation projects for highways, roads, bridges, airports, ports, rail, and storm drainage systems for the departments of transportation, regional transit, airport, port, water, and railroads authorities. The Building Solutions segment offers residential and commercial concrete foundations for single-family and multi-family homes, parking structures, elevated slabs, and other concrete work for developers and general contractors, as well as plumbing and surveys services for residential builds. It operates in the United States, primarily across the Southern, Northeastern, Mid-Atlantic and Rocky Mountain regions, and the Pacific Islands. The company was formerly known as Sterling Construction Company, Inc. and changed its name to Sterling Infrastructure, Inc. in June 2022. Sterling Infrastructure, Inc. was founded in 1955 and is headquartered in The Woodlands, Texas.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph A. Cutillo | CEO, President & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $3.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 7K people. Revenue per employee of $356K ranks in the below the sector median among Industrials peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $52K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 11\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Sterling Infrastructure, Inc. is a mid-cap industrials business with a $8.3B market cap on $2.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +12% over the past three years and +15% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 10% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $363M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 23\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.9%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.3% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Heavy insider selling (net $93.2M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-93226198.0},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Industrials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Supply chain reshoring costs and labour shortages \u2014 onshoring mandates raise capex requirements while a shrinking skilled-labour pool inflates operating costs.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 30% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Industrials peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Sterling Infrastructure (STRL) Down 30.2% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Rebound?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/sterling-infrastructure-strl-down-30-153024616.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795793424.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Is Sterling Infrastructure (STRL) a Buy as Wall Street Analysts Look Optimistic?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036496/is-sterling-infrastructure-strl-a-buy-as-wall-street-analysts-look-optimistic?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Caverage_broker_rating-3036496","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795786202.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.318,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sterling Infrastructure (STRL) Highlights US$7b Backlog, Is The Stock 62% Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/capital-goods/nasdaq-strl/sterling-infrastructure/news/sterling-infrastructure-strl-highlights-us7b-backlog-is-the","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795763512.492,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.625,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Sterling Infrastructure (STRL) Gets $585 Price Target From JPMorgan","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/sterling-infrastructure-strl-gets-585-161505268.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795623305.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875